2.5 P.2.5 Watson integrals
Watson (1939) computed three triple integrals, one for each cubic Bravais lattice. The one relevant to FTD is the BCC integral:
\[
I_{\text{BCC}} = \frac{1}{\pi^3} \int_0^\pi \!\! \int_0^\pi \!\! \int_0^\pi \frac{dk_1 \, dk_2 \, dk_3}{1 - \cos k_1 \cos k_2 \cos k_3} = \frac{\Gamma(1/4)^4}{4\pi^3}
\tag{P.11}
\]
The key identity: \[
\frac{\Gamma(1/4)^4}{4\pi^3} = \frac{G^{*2}}{2\pi}
\tag{P.12}
\]
connecting the BCC Green’s function to the bridge constant.

8.5 Theorem 6.1 (Watson–\(G^*\) identity)
